  "model_authored_rationale": "Iterated local search (ILS) for 320-point Euclidean TSP, compiled with numba.\n\nRationale (exploratory, not yet measured on this split): the common reference is\nnearest-neighbour construction plus best-improvement 2-opt, capped at 300 moves,\nkept as the best of 24 restarts. That typically lands several percent above\noptimal. This method keeps a local optimum and tries to improve it:\n  * Neighbour-list (K=10) 2-opt and Or-opt local search. Or-opt moves segments of\n    1-3 cities in either orientation. Don't-look bits are implemented as a work\n    queue, so only cities near a change are rechecked.\n  * Perturbation is a localized double-bridge (swap two adjacent short segments).\n    A result is accepted when it is no longer than the current tour.\n  * Instances run two at a time via numba prange (2 cores). Each pair gets a\n    wall-time share of the budget, and the budget adapts to the time left.\nEvery output tour is checked to be a permutation; otherwise a NN tour is returned.\nLimitations: time-based iteration counts make results depend slightly on\nmachine speed; no learned component is used.",
